01:22:42.300 --> 01:22:49.100
have lima beans and more lima beans and fruit roll-ups. Then my cousins would put the lima

01:22:49.100 --> 01:22:55.120
beans inside the fruit roll-ups. And we had black olives and we had green olives and we had

01:22:55.120 --> 01:22:59.400
yellow olives and we had clear olives. And sometimes my Aunt Niska would prepare her

01:22:59.400 --> 01:22:59.980
A potato cat.

01:23:00.030 --> 01:23:02.890
But without the potatoes. Or the casserole.

01:23:03.160 --> 01:23:05.640
Did you have a Christmas treat when you were growing up, Nasty?

01:23:05.880 --> 01:23:09.240
Not per se. But one year, my Uncle Yuban had a plan.

01:23:09.440 --> 01:23:13.720
He would venture out into the forest and bring back a majestic 20-foot spruce.

01:23:14.160 --> 01:23:14.880
A hero.

01:23:15.180 --> 01:23:17.720
Ah, he went the wrong way, though, and we never saw him again.

01:23:18.160 --> 01:23:20.520
Crazy Uncle Yuban. Very bad with directions.

01:23:21.060 --> 01:23:24.260
Overall, it sounds like you had some great holiday seasons growing up.

01:23:25.160 --> 01:23:25.520
Nope.

01:23:25.960 --> 01:23:29.970
Stick around. You never know what's...

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:33.880
coming your way next, like Czinska Molnick and his brother Randy.

01:23:36.250 --> 01:23:39.630
Next week on Spangoolie, are you ready for some culture?

01:23:40.780 --> 01:23:42.660
Okay, how about some terror?

01:23:44.240 --> 01:23:48.480
It's the 1943 classic Phantom of the Opera on the next Spangoolie.

01:23:48.640 --> 01:23:50.360
Saturday night on MeTV.

01:23:51.520 --> 01:23:56.330
And now the conclusion of Saturday the 14th.

01:24:05.720 --> 01:24:19.950
It's what we call a fix her up for him.

01:24:25.070 --> 01:24:26.110
It's a little boy.

01:25:03.070 --> 01:25:18.050
my neck. Found him? We looked everywhere. In one minute, terrible things are going to happen.

01:25:20.330 --> 01:25:26.000
Less than a minute? We are doomed!

01:25:47.270 --> 01:25:59.870
This is what you've been looking

01:26:00.090 --> 01:26:08.140
Don't touch that boy. Give me that book.

01:26:08.350 --> 01:26:09.760
Not so fast.

01:26:11.220 --> 01:26:12.960
We have no time to...

01:26:14.210 --> 01:26:15.430
Ready, my boy?

01:26:16.240 --> 01:26:17.320
Will you find me?

01:26:17.920 --> 01:26:19.580
Hand me the book.

01:26:20.060 --> 01:26:21.430
Get in the... Billy?

01:26:21.830 --> 01:26:23.810
He's the only one who can get rid of the monsters.

01:26:24.340 --> 01:26:25.300
He is the monster.

01:26:25.820 --> 01:26:26.440
Give me the book.

01:26:26.720 --> 01:26:29.440
I know who you are. You're in this book. They showed me.

01:26:30.410 --> 01:26:32.290
It can make you very strong.

01:26:32.610 --> 01:26:33.010
Never!

01:26:44.930 --> 01:26:45.890
Quit fooling around.

01:26:47.930 --> 01:26:50.050
The powers are nothing compared to mine.

01:26:50.480 --> 01:26:53.520
When I get that book, I will rule the world.

01:26:54.110 --> 01:26:54.750
Think of it.

01:26:55.460 --> 01:26:55.980
Famine.

01:26:56.540 --> 01:26:56.940
War.

01:26:57.980 --> 01:26:59.280
Those we've got.

01:27:00.000 --> 01:27:02.260
And you will be the first time.

01:27:50.090 --> 01:27:51.610
It was your mother's tangle, horses.

01:28:52.330 --> 01:28:55.800
So over, we have risen again.

01:28:56.600 --> 01:28:56.700
Come.

01:29:00.830 --> 01:29:02.470
get any creepier than this.

01:29:02.610 --> 01:29:20.750
It's gonna be fine.

01:29:43.110 --> 01:29:43.830
Till...

01:30:25.950 --> 01:30:28.350
Destroying the book would free the monster.

01:30:34.540 --> 01:30:35.580
That wasn't the way it worked.

01:30:37.060 --> 01:30:37.860
Thank you for coming.

01:30:40.610 --> 01:30:41.130
Thank you.

01:30:50.050 --> 01:30:53.490
Oh, uh, uh, uh, uh, swell party.

01:30:55.470 --> 01:30:56.130
A nice day.

01:30:56.760 --> 01:30:57.180
You too.

01:30:59.240 --> 01:30:59.880
We don't know who.

01:31:01.370 --> 01:31:02.510
Well, at least he's gone.

01:31:04.830 --> 01:31:06.010
Good boy.

01:31:06.370 --> 01:31:06.770
Good.

01:31:07.640 --> 01:31:09.800
I think they've had enough of this house.

01:31:10.060 --> 01:31:11.160
I think so, too.

01:31:11.660 --> 01:31:14.770
It's time they lived happily ever after.

01:31:16.360 --> 01:31:17.400
And us, too?

01:31:18.240 --> 01:31:20.750
Of course, darling.

01:31:36.780 --> 01:31:38.800
I said the Hyatt's got what they wanted in the end.

01:31:39.000 --> 01:31:42.080
I love that holiday tradition where folks get what they want.

01:31:42.670 --> 01:31:44.910
No more roommates, no more roommates, no more roommates.

01:31:45.840 --> 01:31:46.480
What's that, Gwen?

01:31:47.480 --> 01:31:47.980
Never mind.

01:31:48.220 --> 01:31:50.020
I'm just glad they've got my two front teeth.

01:31:50.180 --> 01:31:53.220
Did you hear about the unfortunate child that was suffering without them?

01:31:55.430 --> 01:31:56.660
Yep, that bites.

01:31:56.900 --> 01:31:58.040
No, it doesn't, Gwen Gulley.

01:31:58.200 --> 01:31:59.840
For you see, without his two front teeth...

01:32:00.480 --> 01:32:03.500
Anyway, I'd like to start a new tradition with you this year.

01:32:03.600 --> 01:32:06.400
It's time for the White Elephant in the Room Gift Exchange!

01:32:07.360 --> 01:32:09.820
I thought we decided to skip gift giving this year.

01:32:10.060 --> 01:32:13.200
That's why I'm calling it the White Elephant in the Room Gift Exchange.

01:32:13.500 --> 01:32:14.680
Isn't this awkward and uncomfortable?

01:32:15.000 --> 01:32:19.230
You are correct! This feeling very much captures the holidays of my youth.

01:32:19.450 --> 01:32:20.910
Go ahead! Take a look inside!

01:32:24.920 --> 01:32:25.620
...or the sticks.

01:32:27.280 --> 01:32:29.440
You got us chew toys! Oh boy!

01:32:31.788 --> 01:32:33.108
They're banshee branches.

01:32:33.948 --> 01:32:35.708
What is this banshee branch?

01:32:35.848 --> 01:32:37.468
They're my latest thrilling invention.

01:32:37.908 --> 01:32:40.808
Whatever happened to giving people sensible socks for the holidays?

01:32:41.188 --> 01:32:41.888
Here's how they work.

01:32:42.476 --> 01:32:45.456
folks love cuddling up close to the fireplace when it's cold outside.

01:32:45.836 --> 01:32:48.956
Especially when someone leaves the dungeon door open in December.

01:32:49.316 --> 01:32:51.176
Okay, you told me there were bats in my belfry.

01:32:51.296 --> 01:32:52.956
I wanted to give them some fresh air.

01:32:53.216 --> 01:32:55.716
Well, this will help make your blood boil even more.

01:32:55.976 --> 01:32:59.996
Just toss your sappy banshee branch into the roaring fireplace and...

01:33:07.750 --> 01:33:12.350
I bet this would taste better with some cowbell.
